										},
										"text": {
											"value_i18n": {
												"en_US": "It started with a rental counter in a garage."
											}
										}
									}
								},
								{
									"id": "split-text",
									"value": {
										"fragmentLink": {
										},
										"text": {
											"value_i18n": {
												"en_US": "<p>Evergreen Outfitters began as a single rental counter in a Portland garage, loaning out patched tents and third-hand stoves to neighbors headed for the Columbia Gorge. The gear came back muddy, the stories came back better, and the counter became a shop.</p><p>Three decades later the garage is a cannery building on Alder Street, but the deal is the same: honest advice, fair prices, and gear we would carry ourselves.</p>"
											}
										}
									}
								},
								{
